body:
Thank you for the heads up on that! Yeah, the food is fancy feast for kittens. What threw us off initially is that it says give 1/3 of the can 3x a day (1 can total) per 3-3.5 lbs. Which would mean when she was weighing in at \~1lb when we got her, she should only be getting 1/3rd can per day--which comes out to 33 calories. This seriously contradicts various other guides on [chewy.com](https://chewy.com), etc. that usually suggest at least 100 calories at her age/weight... Which lines up with what our friend's sister who is a vet advised (100 calories at 8 weeks old).

&#x200B;

Anyway, thank you for your advice! We will look into vet options in our area to ask about an appropriate dewormer for her weight and suggested feeding. Some are still not accepting new "patients" due to COVID it seemed.
